.TH VJOURNAL "1" "March 2026" "vjournal 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vjournal \- manual page for vjournal 1.0
.SH DESCRIPTION
usage: vjournal [global options] [action] [options]
actions:
.TP
edit\-journal
edit journal for given or current date
.TP
edit\-template
edit template
.TP
show\-journal
show journal
.TP
show\-template
show template
.TP
edit
infer edit operation smartly
.TP
show
infer show operation smartly
.TP
cat
concatenate give journal/template
.TP
list
list contents of a directory (see \fB\-\-full\-help\fR)
.TP
delete
delete given journal/template
.TP
rename
rename given journal/template
.TP
copy
copy given journal/template
.SS "options:"
.TP
\fB\-j\fR|\-\-journal
select journal
.TP
\fB\-l\fR|\-\-log
select log
.TP
\fB\-t\fR|\-\-template
select template
.TP
\fB\-u\fR|\-\-use
use given content
.SS "global options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-loglevel\fR
set loglevel (0\-4)
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
enable verbose mode (loglevel 3)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
disable pager
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR
enable colors for subsequent operation
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
disable colors for subsequent operation
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show package version
.TP
\fB\-\-author\fR
show author name
.TP
\fB\-\-tree\-view\fR
tree view of journal directory
.TP
\fB\-\-license\fR
show license of this tool
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR
show repo url
.TP
\fB\-\-about\fR
show metadata about this package
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
show this help
.SS "notes:"
.IP
journals live here (\fI\,/dt/dt/dev/journals\/\fP).
\&'edit\-journal', 'edit\-template', 'edit\-log' can be used to create new
.IP
entries and immediately edit em. afterwards just 'edit' is fine.
starter example: vjournal edit\-log day=today \fB\-t\fR default \fB\-c\fR 'special day: ...'
.IP
\&'edit' and 'show' are more generic, so only existing
.IP
entries can be edited or shown.
.IP
Supports consistent task separated actions: edit\-*, copy\-*, move\-*, rename\-* & delete\-* .
when creating a journal; '\-t' and '\-u' are often interchangeable
.HP
\fB\-u\fR takes priority when both given
.IP
when creating a template; '\-t' may specify a name; '\-u' provides initial content
.IP
(literal strings, file path, or another template)
.IP
comments can be attached to any logs/journal/template.
day= syntax allows specifying the journal date flexibly:
.TP
day=tomorrow / day=yesterday
\-> GNU\-style relative days, (any valid `date \fB\-d\fR 'string'`)
.TP
day=+N
\-> GNU\-style N days relative to today
.TP
day=+Nd / day=\-Nd
\-> BSD\-style relative days (with \fB\-v\fR)
.TP
day='\-v +3d'
\-> raw date flags passed directly (advanced usage)
.SS "examples:"
.IP
# creating and editing journals/templates
.IP
# create/re\-use journal and edit
.IP
vjournal edit\-journal todo
vjournal edit todo # afterwards just 'edit' is fine
.IP
# create/re\-use and edit journal with default template
.IP
vjournal edit\-journal todo \fB\-t\fR default
.IP
# create/re\-use template and edit using default template
.IP
vjournal edit\-template template1 \fB\-t\fR default
.IP
# fill existing template to new journal
.IP
vjournal edit\-journal todo\-project \fB\-t\fR t1
.IP
# create custom templates
.IP
# create blank template (no content)
.IP
vjournal edit\-template
.IP
# create new default (template0) template using default contents (supports \fB\-\-comment\fR)
.IP
vjournal edit\-template \fB\-t\fR default \fB\-u\fR default
.IP
# delete / copy / rename / listing & viewing
.IP
# file navigation
.TP
vjournal copy life life_backup
# clone life
.TP
vjournal delete life
# delete life :(
.TP
vjournal rename life_backup life
# revive life :)
.IP
# pretty print the content of journal or template
.TP
vjournal show todo\-project
# pager enabled by default
.IP
vjournal \fB\-\-no\-pager\fR show todo\-project # disable pager
vjournal cat todo\-project             # concatenate
.IP
# list content of known directories (available options: logs/journals/templates)
.TP
vjournal list logs
# dated logs in logs/ dir with comments
.IP
# extras
.IP
# create new & use default template & add a inline comment
.IP
vjournal edit\-journal project\-work \fB\-t\fR default \fB\-c\fR 'projects related plans'
.IP
# create new & use given template & add a inline comment
.IP
vjournal edit\-journal prod\-script \fB\-t\fR \fI\,/path/to/my/template_file\/\fP \fB\-c\fR 'design and behaviour of prod script'
